---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy | Online Model Cost"
  description="Model Cost runs token and cost math in your browser. Prompts are not uploaded. Currency and theme preference may be stored locally."
>
  <main id="main" class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>What we collect.</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The token calculator keeps your prompt in this tab
        (<code>model-cost-prompt</code>) while you move between pages, so it is
        still there if you open the API cost page or rates and come back. After
        you calculate, the last token counts
        (<code>model-cost-token-handoff</code>) are kept the same way so the
        API cost page can fill input even from the header. Refreshing the page
        or closing the tab clears that copy. Counting and pricing run on your
        device. We do not upload the text to a server.
      </p>
      <p>
        The API cost calculator only uses the numbers you type. Those numbers
        also stay in this browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you switch display currency or color theme, this site may store
        those choices in local storage on your device
        (<code>model-cost-currency</code>, <code>model-cost-theme</code>).
        Those values do not leave the browser. You can clear them with the rest
        of site data for this origin.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is static pages. It does not create an account, and it does
        not need a login. Catalog rates are baked into the page from a public
        price list; fetching those rates for a rebuild is separate from your
        use of the calculators.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hosting and the browser may still see that you requested a page (IP
        address, user agent), as with any website. That is not a copy of your
        prompt.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site uses Google Analytics (measurement ID
        <code>G-B525W1779S</code>) to count page views. Google may receive the
        page URL, approximate location, and device details. Calculator prompts
        and token counts are not sent as analytics events.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions: see <a href="/contact">Contact</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
